~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Uses the trained model from step 04 to predict how strongly each FDA-approved drug would inhibit
  the parasite enzyme         TgDHFR (Toxoplasma gondii dihydrofolate reductase), without doing
  any lab work (virtual screening).
  1) Load the model. 2) Measure how similar each drug is to the training molecules (Applicability
  Domain: the model is         only trustworthy for molecules similar to those it was trained on);
  drugs far from them are still scored, but flagged.         3) Drop drugs that are very large (MW
  above the limit) or contain atoms outside the allowed set (H, C, N, O, F, P, S,         Cl, Br,
  I). 4) Predict pIC50. 5) Report and export the ranking with each drug's similarity to the
  training set.
  pIC50 = -log10(IC50 in molar). Higher means more potent: 6 is IC50 = 1 uM, 7 is 100 nM, 8 is 10
  nM.         Candidates are later confirmed by docking (step 07) and filtered for drug-
  likeness/safety (step 08).
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

