~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] Applicability Domain
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Prediction error grows as a molecule becomes less similar to the training set (Sheridan et al.,
  2004). Each FDA drug         is given its mean Tanimoto similarity to its 5 most similar
  training molecules. A drug is flagged as inside the         domain when that value is at least
  0.638, which is 1 - (mean + 0.5 standard deviations) of the         same distance measured for
  the 859 training molecules against each other (Sahigara et al., 2012). The         multiplier is
  arbitrary: the literature gives no rule for it. No drug is excluded on this flag; it is reported
  with         every candidate, because predictions outside the domain are extrapolations.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

